Changed for Inkwell 0.2 on 2026-09-30, in build.rs and Cargo.toml only:

- Static builds link sherpa-onnx's no-TTS prebuilt libraries (the
  *-static-no-tts-lib archives of the v1.13.4 release) and no longer link
  piper_phonemize, espeak-ng or ucd. Why: those three are sherpa-onnx's
  text-to-speech front end, which Inkwell never used, and espeak-ng is
  GPL-3.0. As published, this crate linked them into every static build.
- Every archive is checked against a sha256 pinned in build.rs before it is
  unpacked. A mismatch, or an archive with no pinned digest, fails the
  build. Why: as published, the crate downloads the archives from GitHub at
  build time and unpacks them without any check.
- As a result, static Linux aarch64 is not supported (v1.13.4 publishes no
  no-TTS archive for it) and shared builds fail (no shared archive is
  pinned). Inkwell 0.2 builds neither.
- An unpacked tree left by an earlier build is used again only if it
  carries the marker a checked unpack writes last (.sha256-verified, holding
  the pin); otherwise it is unpacked again from a checked archive. Why: an
  interrupted unpack or a directory from elsewhere would otherwise be linked
  unchecked.
- SHERPA_ONNX_LIB_DIR is refused. Why: it links a directory nothing checks.
- Cargo.toml adds sha2 as a build dependency, for that check.

Every other file is as published, except upstream's Cargo.lock, which was
removed: a path dependency never uses it. Cargo.toml.orig is upstream's and
plays no part in this build.
